<title>GREECE: CITIBANK, ATHENS CUTS BASE LOAN RATES BY 50 BPS.</title>
<headline>CITIBANK, ATHENS CUTS BASE LOAN RATES BY 50 BPS.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Citibank will cut its base lending</p>
<p>rates for working capital, freely investioble funds and business</p>
<p>and professional loans by 50 basis points effective February 18</p>
<p>it said.</p>
<p>Citibank, which reviews its rates weekly, offers the</p>
<p>following rate structure:</p>
<p>** Base rate for working capital loans at 16.25 from 16.75</p>
<p>percent</p>
<p>** Business and professional base lending rate at 17.00 from</p>
<p>17.50 percent</p>
<p>** Base rate for freely investible funds at 16.50 from 17.0</p>
<p>percent</p>
<p>** Mortgage rate at 16 percent</p>
<p>** Personal installment loans at 23 percent</p>
<p>** Personal installment loans with invoices at 21 percent</p>
<p>** Auto loans at 18.75 percent</p>
<p>Contribution under Law 128 is not included in the rates</p>
<p>quoted, it said.</p>
<p>Base rates on working capital loans in foreign currency for</p>
<p>the coming week will be:</p>
<p>    US Dollars     :  7.99 percent</p>
<p>    Marks	    :  5.69 percent</p>
<p>    Yen		:  3.00 percent</p>
<p>    Guilders	 :  5.50 percent</p>
<p>    Ecu		:  6.60 percent</p>
<p>    Pounds Sterling:  8.81 percent</p>
<p>    French francs  :  5.81 percent</p>
<p>    Swiss francs   :  4.20 percent</p>
<p>--George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
